# Rocci's compilation model

**Prerequisites:** [What is Rocci?](/docs/start/what-is-rocci/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [Generated Roc](/docs/reference/language/generated-roc/) or
[pure components](/docs/concepts/pure-components/).

A `.rocci` file is a Roc module. Rocci recognizes a closed set of `@`
declarations at the start of a top-level definition. Everything else is copied
into generated Roc unchanged.

```text
authored .rocci
    │ parse template regions, copy Roc regions
    ▼
generated .roc  ── Roc type-check and compile ── native host
    │
    └── source-map segments point diagnostics back at the template
```

Rocci does **not** type-check Roc expressions in interpolations, params, or
directive headers. A template can parse and still fail in `roc`. Inspect
source-map segments with `rocci inspect`.

Lowering is syntax, not a component runtime. Tags become `Html.*` calls.
Component tags become ordinary Roc functions. Datastar actions inject
`import Datastar` when missing.

The template crate does not start HTTP or open a window. `rocci-cli` compiles
the generated module and serves it. The preview webview loads that same origin.

Contributor crate maps and AST inspect tags live in
[the tree appendix](/docs/reference/contributor/rocci-tree/), not this page.

**Related:** [File structure](/docs/reference/language/file-structure/),
[Why Roc](/docs/concepts/why-roc/).
